55,87,61,17,10,18,17,87,12,16,16,3,374,17779,553,400,87,488,220,20,3,374,400,19,12947,220,7379,400,74,2418,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nThe remainder when $kx^4+9x^3+kx^2+32x-11$ is divided by $x + 5$ is $4$.  Find $k.$","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"ea7a3fac64cc9e5bfe1d0b9228ff08748db87a8592f899a8ed6b78bdc252efb5"},"seconds":34.34099864959717,"seed":545006515955072820,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve the problem, we will use the Remainder Theorem. According to the Remainder Theorem, if a polynomial \\( f(x) \\) is divided by \\( x - a \\), the remainder is \\( f(a) \\). In this problem, we are given that the remainder when the polynomial \\( kx^4 + 9x^3 + kx^2 + 32x - 11 \\) is divided by \\( x + 5 \\) is 4. This means that when we substitute \\( x = -5 \\) into the polynomial, the result should be 4.\n\nLet's denote the polynomial by \\( f(x) = kx^4 + 9x^3 + kx^2 + 32x - 11 \\). According to the Remainder Theorem, we have:\n\\[ f(-5) = 4. \\]\n\nNow, we substitute \\( x = -5 \\) into the polynomial:\n\\[ f(-5) = k(-5)^4 + 9(-5)^3 + k(-5)^2 + 32(-5) - 11. \\]\n\nLet's calculate each term step-by-step:\n\\[ (-5)^4 = 625, \\]\n\\[ (-5)^3 = -125, \\]\n\\[ (-5)^2 = 25, \\]\n\\[ 32(-5) = -160. \\]\n\nSubstituting these values back into the expression for \\( f(-5) \\), we get:\n\\[ f(-5) = k(625) + 9(-125) + k(25) + (-160) - 11. \\]\n\\[ f(-5) = 625k - 1125 + 25k - 160 - 11. \\]\n\\[ f(-5) = 650k - 1296. \\]\n\nWe know that \\( f(-5) = 4 \\), so we can set up the equation:\n\\[ 650k - 1296 = 4. \\]\n\nTo find \\( k \\), we solve the equation:\n\\[ 650k - 1296 = 4, \\]\n\\[ 650k = 4 + 1296, \\]\n\\[ 650k = 1300, \\]\n\\[ k = \\frac{1300}{650}, \\]\n\\[ k = 2. \\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\( k \\) is \\(\\boxed{2}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{2}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
